\begin{proof}
  \uses{lem:order_fun_field, thm:ord_max_imp_RCF, cor:RCF_ac}
  Let $C$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic 0. Observe that the prime subfield $\mathbb{Q}$ can be ordered. Further, given an ordered subfield $F$ with $\bar{F}\neq C$, we can use Lemma \ref{lem:order_fun_field} to adjoin an element transcendental over $F$, obtaining a strictly bigger ordered subfield.

  Apply Zorn's lemma to obtain a maximal ordered subfield $R\subseteq C$; then $\bar{R}=C$. By Theorem \ref{thm:ord_max_imp_RCF}, $R$ must be real closed. By Corollary \ref{cor:RCF_ac}, $C\cong R(i)$, and so $[C:R]=2$.
\end{proof}

